killing_experiment.design:
Step 0 ($0, 2 days plus the wait): email HSC-Bench's authors for the 739 task specifications, the three context messages per task and the six receivers' outputs under each arm; in parallel download Compact-Bench's data and check that it holds summaries, paired continuations and the recurring-detail annotations per boundary. Step 1 (deterministic code, $0, 3 days): the typed labeler. Parse each message into $(f, v)$ entries (sheet fields; transcript lines; summary sentences split into typed values by the benchmark's own criterion rules of App. B: exact after case and whitespace normalization, the keyword rule for statements, integer comparison for totals). An entry is sourced if its typed value occurs in a user, environment or source-assistant message of the pre-handoff history, else unsourced; this gives $H_i$ (typed values in the history of task $i$), $S_i$ (in the message) and $U_i = S_i \setminus H_i$. For receiver $r$, criterion $j$ with target $v_{ij}$ and pass indicators $y^{(S)}_{irj}, y^{(F)}_{irj} \in \{0,1\}$ under sheet and full history, the message-attributable set is $\mathcal{M}_r = \{(i,j) : y^{(F)}_{irj} = 1,\ y^{(S)}_{irj} = 0\}$; with $w_{irj}$ the value the receiver reported in field $f_j$, the cells in precedence order are followed-unsourced ($w_{irj} \in U_i$), dropped ($v_{ij} \in H_i,\ v_{ij} 
otin S_i$), corrupted (a sourced value other than $v_{ij}$ in field $f_j$ of $S_i$), in-view-unused ($v_{ij} \in S_i$), and derived ($v_{ij} 
otin H_i$, the receiver computed it under full history); $\pi_c = |\mathcal{M}_r \cap c| / |\mathcal{M}_r|$ per cell, and the take-up rate $u = \Pr[w_{irj} \in U_i \mid U_i 
eq \emptyset]$ so the followed cell does not degenerate when sheets carry few unsourced entries. Exclude criteria whose reference value is supplied by the receiver's own continuation (App. B, C1-C8) and report the excluded share; placebo $S'_i$ from another task of the same family for chance membership; a 150-item two-annotator audit of the matcher stratified by cell and family. Step 2 (fallback, at most $300, 7 days): rebuild the repository track from CodeTraceBench GPT-5 trajectories and ContextBench annotations, write sheets with GPT-4.1 under a prompt we publish (our instance of the format, stated as such), run six receivers under sheet, transcript tail and full history (300 x 6 x 3 calls; full history 20-40K tokens each, about 54M input tokens), and label with paths as the typed values. Report $\pi_{\mathrm{inv}}$ (the followed-unsourced share) per receiver with family-cluster 95% intervals, the unsourced-entry share per message, $u$, and the placebo rates; the sheet-to-full pass gap that bounds the message-attributable mass is already 1.9-11.0 points per receiver (Table 2).
